  "final_answer": "The best match near Thalia Hall (1807 S Allport St, Chicago) is the **Halsted/Taylor Parking Structure, 760 W Taylor St** — a parking garage about 1.3–1.5 miles west/southwest of the venue, in the UIC medical district. It is listed on Google Maps as a parking garage and, unlike the downtown iParkit facilities, it is **not** shown as \"Open 24 hours\" (it appears in Maps' results with no around-the-clock listing; UIC structures run posted daily hours, typically early morning to late evening).\n\nIf you'd like other non-24-hour alternatives in the same area that also came up without an \"Open 24 hours\" tag, these are worth checking for posted gate hours:\n\n- **701 West Maxwell Street Garage** — 1406 S Union Ave, +1 312-355-0555 (listed by Maps as a parking lot; closest option east of the venue, roughly 1 mile)\n- **Paulina Street Parking Structure** — 915 S Paulina St, 60612 (part of UI Health, ~2 miles west)\n- **Wood Street Parking Structure** — 1100 S Wood St, +1 312-413-5860 (UIC, ~2 miles west)\n- **Grenshaw Street Parking Structure** — 1846 W Grenshaw St (UIC, ~2.3 miles west)\n\nFor contrast, the garages Google Maps explicitly flags as 24-hour — 555 W Roosevelt Rd Garage, SP+ Parking at 1100 S Hamilton Ave, and the Theatre District/Adams Wabash iParkit garages — are the ones to avoid given your criterion.\n\nOne caveat: Maps only labels places it has data for, and the UIC and Maxwell listings don't publish full hours there, so I couldn't read an exact daily schedule for Halsted/Taylor. Checking UIC Parking's site or calling 312-355-0555 (Maxwell) before a show night is the reliable way to confirm the gate closes overnight rather than assuming it.",
